      ],
      "application_cycle": "rolling",
      "next_deadline": "Apply to Lift to Rise directly; County funds are capital contributions, not a County application process.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "false",
      "layering_notes": "Riverside County's Housing and Workforce Solutions (HWS) department runs the Urban County HUD programs, PLHA, HHAP, Homekey+ sponsorships and project loans, while the Housing Authority of the County of Riverside (HACR, same Board sitting as Commissioners) supplies project-based vouchers, housing successor funds and land; rivcohws.org and harivco.org block automated access, so records were built from Board of Supervisors files on riversidecountyca.iqm2.com and media.rivcocob.org, RUHS Behavioral Health, the Assessor and the County Housing Element. The Catalyst Fund is the only revolving predevelopment source in the eastern county and is often the first money into Coachella and Indio tax credit deals before County PLHA, HOME and HACR PBVs; the fund itself and CVAG's housing programs belong in Pass 4 and Pass 3. Source is the County news release on the 2022 contribution; FY 2026-27 budget action at rivco.gov/node/7036.",
      "source_url": "https://rivco.gov/node/589",
